## Bug

When an iMessage user sends a rich link (the iOS "rich link" preview bubble that appears when you share a URL), the Photon sidecar does not normalize it and the Python adapter falls through to a catch-all branch, producing:

```
[Photon content type not handled: richlink]
```

The agent never sees the URL, title, or any useful payload — just the placeholder string.

## Root cause

Two gaps:

### 1. Sidecar (`plugins/platforms/photon/sidecar/index.mjs`)

`normalizeContent()` has no case for `content.type === "richlink"`. It falls through to:

```js
return { type: content.type || "unknown" };
```

So the NDJSON event sent to Python carries `{ type: "richlink" }` with no URL, title, or summary.

The spectrum-ts SDK defines richlink content as:
- `url: string` (required)
- `title: () => Promise<string | undefined>` (async accessor)
- `summary: () => Promise<string | undefined>` (async accessor)
- `cover: () => Promise<...>` (async accessor, optional cover image)

### 2. Python adapter (`plugins/platforms/photon/adapter.py`)

The `else` branch at line ~621 catches it:

```python
text = f"[Photon content type not handled: {ctype}]"
```

No richlink case exists to extract the URL and format it as text.

## Impact

Any iMessage user who sends a rich link to their Hermes agent gets a useless placeholder instead of the URL. This is a common interaction — iOS automatically converts shared URLs to rich links.

## Fix

### Sidecar — add richlink case to `normalizeContent()`:

```js
if (content.type === "richlink") {
  const out = { type: "richlink", url: content.url || "" };
  if (typeof content.title === "function") {
    try {
      const title = await content.title();
      if (title) out.title = title;
    } catch { /* accessor may fail if metadata fetch did not complete */ }
  } else if (typeof content.title === "string") {
    out.title = content.title;
  }
  if (typeof content.summary === "function") {
    try {
      const summary = await content.summary();
      if (summary) out.summary = summary;
    } catch { /* same */ }
  } else if (typeof content.summary === "string") {
    out.summary = content.summary;
  }
  return out;
}
```

### Python adapter — add richlink case before the else branch:

```python
elif ctype == "richlink":
    url = content.get("url") or ""
    title = content.get("title") or ""
    summary = content.get("summary") or ""
    parts = []
    if title:
        parts.append(title)
    if summary and summary != title:
        parts.append(summary)
    if url:
        parts.append(url)
    text = "\n".join(parts) if parts else url or "[Photon richlink with no URL]"
    mtype = MessageType.TEXT
```

## Environment

- Hermes Agent: commit 9f4c0b27c
- spectrum-ts: pinned 3.x
- Platform: macOS 26.5.1
- Channel: Photon iMessage
